# DEVELOPMENT/STABILIZATION CACHE POLICY — deterministic freshness over cache performance while Studio
# is under active development. The server's default static-file policy is public, max-age=604800 (7
# days) — once a browser cached a file under that default, it wouldn't even ask again for up to a week,
# which is what caused "incognito shows the new build, a normal tab doesn't" repeatedly. This FilesMatch
# now covers HTML as well as JS/CSS — the earlier version of this rule only covered \.(js|css)$, which is
# exactly why guest.html/director.html's served content (and the /studio auth-wrapper page) kept being
# served stale even after js/css deploys landed correctly: the page shell itself had no Cache-Control
# header at all and fell through to the 7-day default.
#
# no-store (not just no-cache) is deliberate: no-cache still lets the browser keep a local copy for
# conditional revalidation (an If-Modified-Since round trip, cheap but still a cached copy in play);
# no-store forbids keeping any cached copy at all, so every load is a genuine fresh fetch. This trades
# a small amount of bandwidth/latency for zero ambiguity about whether a device is running the build
# actually deployed — the explicit priority while this app is still under active development. Revisit
# once the churn settles — content-hashed/versioned filenames (real long-lived immutable caching) is
# the eventual production answer, not this.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(html|htm|js|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate"
    Header unset Expires
    Header unset ETag
  </FilesMatch>
  FileETag None
</IfModule>

RewriteEngine On

RewriteRule ^studio$ /studio/director.html [L]

# Bounce direct/top-level requests for director.html back to the auth gate at /studio, but not the
# authenticated app shell's own iframe embed of it (studio-auth.js sets #studioAppFrame's src to
# ./director.html) — THE_REQUEST alone can't tell those apart, so also require Sec-Fetch-Dest to be
# something other than "iframe" before redirecting.
RewriteCond %{HTTP:Sec-Fetch-Dest} !=iframe
RewriteCond %{THE_REQUEST} \s/+studio/director\.html[\s?]
RewriteRule ^studio/director\.html$ /studio [R=302,L]
